    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "Looks like it. I upgraded to jax/jaxlib version 0.4.13, ran the script 50 times, and got NaNs 37/50 times.\r\n\r\nEdit: I should add that this isn't blocking me or anything since I found a more numerically stable way to accumulate the matrix I was using this on. I do wonder if it's possible that this isn't a bug, and it just happens that this matrix is so close to always yielding NaN that GPU non-determinism pushes it one way or the other?",
