  {
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "I was able to reproduce this problem on V100. By printing hashes of the various arrays in the program, I found that it's actually the matrix multiplication `mat @ mat.T` that is nondeterministic. Different matmul algorithms produce slightly different results, and that's enough to prevent the Cholesky decomposition from working in some cases.\r\n\r\nIn principle one should be able fix this by setting `XLA_FLAGS=--xla_gpu_deterministic_ops=1`, but I tried that and it still doesn't work. I filed an XLA:GPU bug (https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/6796).",
    "created_at": "2023-11-06T16:18:43Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/15769#issuecomment-1795333323",
